# {{ n.name }}: MPC node {{ n.id }} on {{ ip_of[n.host] }} (team instructions)

Run by **this node's team** on {{ ip_of[n.host] }}, not by the operator. The operator never sees
this node's passphrase or share.

1. Get `MPC_NODE_TOKEN` from the operator over your secret channel.
2. On {{ ip_of[n.host] }} (the image `{{ mpc_image }}` is already loaded there):

   ```bash
   cp -r {{ repo_dir }}/mpc-signer/deploy/node /opt/mpc-node && cd /opt/mpc-node
   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
   ```

   `.env`:

   ```
   MPC_IMAGE={{ mpc_image }}
   MPC_NODE_ID={{ n.id }}
   MPC_BIND_IP={{ ip_of[n.host] }}
   MPC_NODE_TOKEN=<from the operator>
   MPC_COMPUTE_THREADS=<about the host's core count>
   ```

   ```bash
   ./init.sh
   ```

   Store the generated `MPC_NODE_PASSPHRASE` (in `.env`) in **your team's** vault now.
3. Send `node{{ n.id }}.json` (public keys only) to the operator, who puts it in
   `ansible/state/mpc/node{{ n.id }}.json`.
4. When the operator sends `cluster.json`: compare its `sha256sum` with the operator's
   (second channel), copy it to `/opt/mpc-node/`, then:

   ```bash
   docker compose up -d && docker compose logs --tail 5    # "node loaded", "node API listening"
   ```

5. Backups (hourly, this team's own location):
   `0 * * * * /opt/mpc-node/backup.sh /secure/backup`
